/// Runs an arbitrary SQL query against a database and (optionally) returns the result as
/// an array of objects, one for each row returned.
///
/// If the query fails to execute then the message will remain unchanged and the error can
/// be caught using error handling methods outlined
/// [here](/docs/configuration/error_handling).
///
/// ## Alternatives
///
/// For basic inserts or select queries use either the
/// [`sql_insert`](/docs/components/processors/sql_insert) or the
/// [`sql_select`](/docs/components/processors/sql_select) processor. For more complex
/// queries use the [`sql_raw`](/docs/components/processors/sql_raw) processor.
///
/// Status: deprecated
