/// drivers require question marks (`?`) whereas others expect incrementing dollar signs
/// (`$1`, `$2`, and so on) or colons (`:1`, `:2` and so on). The style to use is outlined
/// in this table:
///
/// | Driver | Placeholder Style |
/// |---|---|
/// | `clickhouse` | Dollar sign |
/// | `mysql` | Question mark |
/// | `postgres` | Dollar sign |
/// | `mssql` | Question mark |
/// | `sqlite` | Question mark |
/// | `oracle` | Colon |
/// | `snowflake` | Question mark |
/// | `spanner` | Question mark |
/// | `trino` | Question mark |
/// | `gocosmos` | Colon |
